<i> The JVC camcorder
 was a huge hit,</i>

00:18:13.625 --> 00:18:15.360
and that just made
other companies

00:18:15.460 --> 00:18:17.096
that much more eager
to try and see

00:18:17.196 --> 00:18:18.630
<i> if they could make
 something better.</i>

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:20.165
Misty:
<i> Sony was making one.</i>

00:18:20.265 --> 00:18:21.500
<i> Panasonic was making one.</i>

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:22.835
<i> They were all just
 hoping to get</i>

00:18:22.935 --> 00:18:24.536
<i> their corner
 of this marketplace.</i>

00:18:24.636 --> 00:18:27.739
<i> Things became lighter,
 easier to use, smaller.</i>

00:18:27.839 --> 00:18:30.542
And then digital came about.

00:18:30.642 --> 00:18:32.878
Man: Now, this is the wave
of the future right here.

00:18:32.978 --> 00:18:34.813
Reporter: All the whiz-bang
production techniques

00:18:34.913 --> 00:18:36.682
that Hollywood studios use

00:18:36.782 --> 00:18:38.183
at a fraction of the cost.

00:18:38.283 --> 00:18:40.285
The camcorder
reached a plateau

00:18:40.385 --> 00:18:42.554
where there was just
no making it any better

00:18:42.654 --> 00:18:46.225
while it was still
for VHS tapes.

00:18:46.325 --> 00:18:47.693
Marques:
<i> So even though the retro look</i>

00:18:47.793 --> 00:18:50.696
<i> of the JVC camcorder
 might seem outdated,</i>

00:18:50.796 --> 00:18:54.867
<i> it's clear to me
 that our content-obsessed
 generation now</i>

00:18:54.967 --> 00:18:57.569
<i> owes a lot
 to this piece of tech.</i>

00:18:57.669 --> 00:18:59.538 align:start size:91% position:9%
What's the legacy
of this JVC camera?

00:18:59.638 --> 00:19:02.141
Goldstein:
<i> Everybody whose phone
 has a camera on it</i>

00:19:02.241 --> 00:19:06.411
is a beneficiary
of the JVC camcorder.

00:19:06.511 --> 00:19:09.581
<i> And you can absolutely
 see the legacy of that</i>

00:19:09.681 --> 00:19:12.918
in today's YouTube stars
shooting things

00:19:13.018 --> 00:19:15.587
<i> from their own lives
 in real time</i>

00:19:15.687 --> 00:19:18.690
with very little technology
and equipment.

00:19:18.790 --> 00:19:20.826
Schafer:
<i> And we live in a time
 with infinite amount</i>

00:19:20.926 --> 00:19:22.528
<i> of user-generated content.</i>

00:19:22.628 --> 00:19:23.929
But if you think about it,

00:19:24.029 --> 00:19:26.765
<i> the very first visual
 user-generated content</i>

00:19:26.865 --> 00:19:28.433
<i> that was massively accessible,</i>

00:19:28.533 --> 00:19:30.669
it exists because
of the VHS camcorder.

00:19:30.769 --> 00:19:34.239
Misty:
<i> People wanted to see
 real-life stuff.</i>

00:19:34.339 --> 00:19:38.744
Without this camera,
there would be no YouTube.

00:19:38.844 --> 00:19:41.813 align:start size:97% position:3%
- You'd be out of a job.
- Yeah, that's exactly right.

00:19:41.913 --> 00:19:45.617
Roberson:
<i> So, the legacy
 of the JVC camcorder</i>

00:19:45.717 --> 00:19:48.287
is a reminder
that we have the ability

00:19:48.387 --> 00:19:50.856
to decide for ourselves
what are important stories.

00:19:53.491 --> 00:19:55.861
<i> The JVC camcorder allowed
 people to justify,</i>

00:19:55.961 --> 00:19:58.931
"Yes, my life is important.
My stories are important."

00:19:59.031 --> 00:20:01.533 align:start size:88% position:13%
